{np}{FF 9C 0101}{FF 8D 0102}{FF 85 013d}Who can know if the path we choose
{FF 8D 0102}is right or wrong?{FF 89 c9}
{FF 8D 0102}
{FF 8D 0102}I will fear no reproach.{FF 89 8d}
{FF 8D 0102}For man is a creature of sorrow and fault,{FF 89 3d}
{FF 8D 0102}and ever will be.{FF 98 0105}

{np}{FF 9C 0101}{FF 8D 0102}{FF 85 013d}At Almorica...{FF 89 47} Those words Leonar spoke to us.{FF 89 b5}
{FF 8D 0102}Did he truly mean what he said?{FF 89 b5}
{FF 8D 0102}Have I done right...{FF 89 3d}or wrong?{FF 98 0104}

{np}{FF 9C 0101}{FF 8D 0102}{FF 85 013d}I may deceive others...{FF 89 8d}
{FF 8D 0102}But never myself.{FF 89 b5}
{FF 8D 0102}Though at times, the temptation is all too great.{FF 98 0105}

{np}{FF 9C 0101}{FF 8D 0102}{FF 85 013d}In the name of the Great Father Philaha,{FF 89 29}
{FF 8D 0102}{FF 85 013d}you are hereby crowned our Sovereign Lord,{FF 89 33}
{FF 8D 0102}{FF 85 013d}Queen Versalia Oberyth,{FF 89 29} Defender of the Realm.{FF 89 5b}
{FF 8D 0102}{FF 85 013d}Let no man gainsay this sanctified ascension.{FF 99 01a1}

{np}{FF 85 011f}I understand how you must feel.{FF 99 018d}{pp}{FF 85 011f}You have done much.{FF 89 3d}
All that was required of you, and of your sisters as well.{FF 89 b5}{pp}{FF 85 011f}But your labors are done on the morn.{FF 89 5b}
Let me shoulder your burden.{FF 89 c9}{pp}{FF 85 011f}You can...{FF 89 29}you can do as you like, for once.{FF 89 51}
Live your own life, Olivya.{FF 99 01ab}

{np}{FF 85 011f}Listen to me, {hero}!{FF 89 3d}
You must save Catiua.{FF 89 ab}{pp}{FF 85 011f}You are the only one who can.{FF 89 5b}
You can lead her to her rightful destiny...{FF 89 dd}{pp}{FF 85 011f}Do this for us...for Valer―{FF 89 3d}*cough*{FF 99 0183}

{np}{FF 85 011f}Ach, no looks from you now.{FF 89 33}
Time to be a man, boy.{FF 89 97}{pp}{FF 85 011f}That's right.{FF 89 29}
Give a grin. Things aren't as bleak as they seem.{FF 99 018d}

{np}{FF 85 011f}It's all right, {hero}.{FF 89 47}
It's all right.{FF 89 8d}{pp}{FF 85 011f}When things settle down here, you should come to Xenobia.{FF 89 3d} We'll be waiting for you.{FF 89 8d}{pp}{FF 85 011f}You should see the wider world.{FF 89 1f}
For Valeria's sake as much as your own.{FF 89 ab}{pp}{FF 85 011f}And for your sister, neh?{FF 89 3d}
Promise me now, you'll come!{FF 99 018d}

{np}{FF 9C 0101}{FF 8D 0102}{FF 85 013d}In the name of the Great Father Philaha,{FF 89 29}
{FF 8D 0102}{FF 85 013d}you are hereby crowned our Sovereign Lord,{FF 89 33}
{FF 8D 0102}{FF 85 013d}King {hero} Morne, Defender of the Realm.{FF 89 5b}
{FF 8D 0102}{FF 85 013d}Let no man gainsay this sanctified ascension.{FF 99 01a1}

{np}{FF 9C 0101}{FF 85 013d}Dearest {hero},{FF 89 65}
{FF 92}By the time you read this,{FF 89 29} we will be crossing the
Obero Sea.{FF 89 3d} I was unable to help you as I would
have liked,{FF 89 29} and yet,{FF 89 3d} I would not trade my time
spent with you for the world.{FF 99 01b5}

{np}{FF 9C 0101}{FF 85 013d}We leave before the coronation,{FF 89 8d}
{FF 92}but there is something I would have you know.{FF 89 79}
―And I will tell you, {FF 89 29}despite my brother's protestations!{FF 99 01b5}

{np}{FF 9C 0101}{FF 85 013d}When Sirene dwelt within me, {FF 89 51}
I dreamt many dreams.{FF 89 97}
Dreams of wars most terrible.{FF 99 01b5}

{np}{FF 9C 0101}{FF 85 013d}I saw a war between peoples in the distant past.{FF 89 5b}
{FF 92}I saw Dorgalua's great war too...{FF 89 29}
And your war.{FF 89 51} I lived them all in dreams.{FF 99 01b5}

{np}{FF 9C 0101}{FF 85 013d}Perhaps the dreams sprang from {pal 16}her{palreset} memories.{FF 89 3d}
Or perhaps they were merely the fancies of an
unmoored mind.{FF 89 65} But I believe what I saw
to be true.{FF 99 01b5}

{np}{FF 9C 0101}{FF 85 013d}There is one that remains with me most.{FF 89 8d}
{FF 92}It was not a vision of wars past,{FF 89 3d}
but of wars future.{FF 89 79}
Though I did not understand it at the time I dreamt
it,{FF 89 3d} its meaning is clear to me now.{FF 99 01b5}

{np}{FF 9C 0101}{FF 85 013d}As our choices in the past affect the future,{FF 89 47}
you have given us more choice than we've ever had
in what is to come.{FF 99 01b5}

{np}{FF 9C 0101}{FF 85 013d}We make haste now for Xenobia,{FF 89 47}
{FF 92}ere the Wheel can turn against us.{FF 89 8d}
Though I do not know if we will succeed,{FF 89 47}
anything is better than sitting upon our hands.{FF 99 01b5}

{np}{FF 9C 0101}{FF 85 013d}I will fight for my homeland,{FF 89 29} and for your
Valeria.{FF 89 47} As will my brother,{FF 89 29} Sir Lanselot,{FF 89 29}
and Sir Warren.{FF 89 47} To the death,{FF 89 29} if need be.{FF 99 01b5}

{np}Who are you, boy, and how is it you know my name?{pp}No matter.
You'll sing once we have you caged.{pp}{pal 16}Forward!{palreset}
Show them what it means to stand in the way of Lodis!
